# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Python virtualenvs (any depth)
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Claude Code scratch
.claude/

# Local SQLite database (user accounts + channel data — keep local only)
backend/aether.db
backend/*.db-journal
backend/*.db-wal
backend/*.db-shm

# Secrets — .env.production is intentionally tracked (Vite-public Sentry DSN
# only, see file header); everything else with real secrets stays out.
.env*
!.env.production
*.pem
id_rsa*
# Local secrets folder (Cloudflare origin cert + key, etc.). The *.pem
# rule already covers those files, but ignore the whole folder so any
# non-pem secret dropped here later also stays out of git.
/secrets/

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
.deploy.local

# Internal operating docs. Cost basis, margins, provider account audits -
# the business side, which is not public even though the code is. They
# stay on disk and ship to the server via deploy.sh so the admin panel
# can still render STACK.md.
STACK.md
ROADMAP.md
docs/STORAGE_BILLING_DESIGN.md
docs/STRIPE_AUDIT.md
docs/CLOUDFLARE_AUDIT.md

# Claude Code's per-machine settings. Local paths, no business in a
# public repo.
.claude/settings.local.json
.env.production

# Internal runbooks. The restore procedure describes how the
# infrastructure is assembled, and the rename audit is a stale migration
# checklist. Useful to run, not useful to publish.
deploy/RESTORE.md
docs/RENAME_AUDIT.md
